This shared read-only factual checker authenticates the reviewed geometry
workflow02/comparer03, actual comparison transport and its closed outer/inner
recorder receipts. Invoke check.py with --source-preparation MANIFEST#SHA,
--comparison-transport RECORD#SHA, --outer-execution RECEIPT#SHA and --output
FRESH_IGNORED_JSON. Root and the independent reviewer may use the same Source
with distinct fresh outputs. The checker does not invoke another module.

It reads every raw gzip artifact and every decoded JSONL row in stored order,
checks raw and decoded hashes/bytes/counts, then reconciles complete mismatch,
required/optional-unavailable and paired-owner ledgers. IDs/names/order are
copied from authenticated Native/Rust observations. All thirteen parser-added
null members and all policy exclusions retain explicit no-PASS markers.

The common factual schema is src06-ordinary-geometry-comparison-factual-review.v1.
ledger_facts has exactly mismatches/unavailable/paired_owners, each containing
only rows/decoded_bytes/decoded_sha256. Report phase counters are retained with
an explicit statement that comparison-call counters were not independently
recomputed. Ledger counts and hashes are independently recomputed in full.

Factual acceptance can describe an actual selected failure or integrity-only
outcome; it never assumes zero mismatches. No geometry equation, endpoint
comparison, engine, comparer or target is run. Full archived Source is checked
without requiring historical Source bytes to remain current canonical files.
Scientific, whole-geometry, ordinary-cadence and gate PASS are not claimed.
